diff --git a/Q6A-SOURCE-PORT.md b/Q6A-SOURCE-PORT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1c512cf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Q6A-SOURCE-PORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Q6A native Codec2 source candidate
+
+This is a source-build candidate. Android compilation, the target driver, ordinary apps and the joint native regression have not passed for these new libraries yet. The currently installed native decoder/H.264 baseline remains the recovery reference.
+
+## Pinned inputs
+
+- Dragon Q6A release: `lineage24-v4`, commit `8af4f9a0fea2a031233d2240e8492e10ee900e1e`.
+- Codec2 source: `LineageOS/android_external_v4l2_codec2`, commit `6685af1c65467d0b550d7b904418f65059bc3cbb`.
+- All six release Codec2 patches are applied before this candidate patch: 0011, 0013, 0014, 0017, 0018 and 0021. Their existing cache, queue, GOP and picture-flag work is retained.
+
+## Candidate behavior
+
+HEVC registration remains property-gated and requires queried Main 8-bit, Main-tier level and geometry capabilities. The initial implementation is limited to CBR, 3840x2160 and 30 fps. It checks requested controls and both queue frame rates, refreshes negotiated formats before buffer allocation, and preserves original driver sync flags. Unsupported configuration is an error.
+
+Bounded VPS/SPS/PPS collection handles separate complete-NAL header callbacks without consuming a picture work item. The first picture receives standard Annex-B `csd-0`. Main 8-bit 4:2:0 geometry and the configured level must match the SPS. This candidate intentionally rejects changed parameter sets and even lower SPS level signaling; stop/reconfigure is required. Byte-fragmented NALs are not supported.
+
+The source port also restores the tested allocator-id17 dma-buf identity path, immutable per-input HEVC HDR snapshots, and fixed BT.709 limited RGB Surface conversion/signaling. YUV copy paths are retained. General matrix/range negotiation and HDR HDMI output remain separate work.
+
+HDR uses public typed buffer metadata with nested structure descriptors and no default-zero queryable HDR descriptor. Host snapshot tests do not prove framework transport or clearing of a previously cached `hdr-static-info` in a single decoder instance. Fresh SDR, HDR changes, HDR-to-SDR in the same instance, held buffers, flush, new CSD and reordered output require explicit application regression. No system reflection binary patch is part of this source change.
+
+## Build and deployment boundaries
+
+Build `libv4l2_codec2_common`, `libv4l2_codec2_components`, `libv4l2_codec2_v4l2` and `libc2plugin_store` against the matching pinned Android platform. The first three must be treated as a coherent set: base class layouts and encoder signatures changed. A single rebuilt library cannot be substituted into the old set.
+
+The build workflow exports libraries only. It does not rebuild or install images, boot files, the kernel, firmware, allocator APEX packages, codec XML or properties. New libraries can differ in size, so the earlier same-size ext4 replacement helper is unsuitable for packaging them. A later separate candidate must preserve raw Android xattrs, the native signed allocator, the pool mask `0xf70000`, existing drivers, data and fallback route. HEVC XML/property activation requires a validated candidate.
+
+## Validation performed before the platform build
+
+Standalone header, HDR snapshot, fixed-color and level-policy checks pass on the host, including address/undefined-behavior instrumentation. Registration and driver-control logic were also checked with narrow external-type/ioctl fixtures. These do not establish Android ABI compatibility or hardware performance. Some restricted test environments require disabling only LeakSanitizer because task-list metadata is unavailable.
+
+Host entry points:
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/host/run_hevc_level_limits.py
+python3 tests/host/run_registration_smoke.py
+sh tests/host/run_hevc_hdr.sh --sanitize
+sh tests/host/run_color_conversion.sh
+```
+
+Header collector build instructions and software-fixture checks are in `tests/hevc_headers/README.md`. The pinned Android interface tests are in `tests/c2_comp_intf/`; they still require the actual platform build.
+
+Before promotion, require ordinary MediaCodec enumeration/selection, short HEVC raw and Surface encode/decode roundtrips, unmodified CSD and MP4 muxing, dimensions/color/timestamps/EOS, sync flags and requested key frames, repeated stop/flush/reconfigure, sustained 900-frame 4K30, then the retained H.264/HDR/five-decoder joint regression. A successful compilation alone is not a device test.
