+# HEVC encoder output headers
+
+The helper has no Android dependency. Build and run its boundary, cross-callback,
+parameter linkage, profile/geometry, lifecycle and malformed-input tests on a host:
+
+```sh
+g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -fsanitize=address,undefined \
+  -fno-omit-frame-pointer -Icommon/include common/HEVCEncoderHeaders.cpp \
+  tests/hevc_headers/HEVCEncoderHeadersTest.cpp -o /tmp/hevc-headers-test
+/tmp/hevc-headers-test
+```
+
+The boundary tests include the exact VPS/SPS/PPS from the successful direct Iris
+capture with stream SHA256
+`8f6da165355b2f7901e34f31f33e1a81724158cdbcb1f10c855371dee474b3fc`.
+They verify both parameter sets' Main profile/Main tier/level153 prefixes,
+cross-callback CSD delivery, and rejection of a modified high-tier VPS.
+The small embedded parameter-set fixture uses a synthetic slice for linkage;
+it does not substitute for independently decoding the captured stream.
+
+A complete software-encoded Main 8-bit 4:2:0 fixture can additionally be checked:
+
+```sh
+ffmpeg -f lavfi -i testsrc2=size=64x64:rate=1 -frames:v 1 -pix_fmt yuv420p \
+  -c:v libx265 -x265-params pools=1:frame-threads=1:repeat-headers=1 \
+  -f hevc /tmp/hevc-main.h265
+/tmp/hevc-headers-test /tmp/hevc-main.h265
+ffmpeg -i /tmp/hevc-main.h265 -f null -
+```
+
+Synthetic SPS unit fixtures cover only the parsed prefix; they are not complete
+conforming bitstreams. The software fixture exercises complete headers. These
+tests do not establish Android ABI compatibility, V4L2 capture behavior, app or
+Surface encoding, hardware performance, or end-to-end conformance.
+The restricted host runner cannot expose the task information required by
+LeakSanitizer; the ASan test harness disables leak scanning only. Address and
+undefined-behavior instrumentation remain enabled.
+
+The producer contract is complete Annex-B NAL units with at most one complete
+picture per nonempty callback. VPS, SPS and PPS may be separate header-only
+callbacks, including timestamp zero. A header-only result must return before
+work/timestamp lookup. The component attaches the normal VPS/SPS/PPS `csd-0` to
+the first VCL work only; it never completes a work for a header packet. Byte-
+fragmented NALs and changes to parameter sets require an explicit error/restart.
+After CSD delivery, flush retains the validated configuration because stream-off
+does not promise that the driver resends it. Stop/start clears all header state.
+The component supplies the configured Main-tier HEVC level ID. Both VPS and SPS
+must independently establish Main profile1, Main tier0 and that exact known
+level, and their general levels must match. The VPS prefix must describe a
+self-contained single-layer stream. A control acknowledgement, or an absent
+tier control, is insufficient evidence of the encoded tier.
+This initial candidate rejects even a lower, otherwise conforming VPS/SPS level
+rather than reporting a configured level different from the observed stream.
