+# Captured driver packet replay
+
+Authenticate the source report/archive and extract its `output.hevc` and
+`records.jsonl` as bounded regular files, then run from this source checkout:
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/host/run_captured_hevc_driver.py --stream /absolute/output.hevc --records /absolute/records.jsonl
+```
+
+`--cxx /path/to/c++` selects the host compiler; otherwise `CXX` or `c++` is used.
+The runner checks the fixed 3840x2160, 32-frame, 30-fps, level153 fixture ledger,
+snapshots the supplied files, and compiles the **current**
+`common/HEVCEncoderHeaders.cpp` and its actual header under ASan/UBSan. No
+parameter-set parser implementation is mirrored in this test. LeakSanitizer is
+disabled because restricted hosts may hide `/proc/<pid>/task`.
+
+The replay requires the observed joined initial VPS/SPS/PPS plus picture,
+32 picture callbacks with the original timestamps, exactly one CSD delivery,
+and one separate empty LAST callback. It deliberately handles that empty drain
+callback outside the header parser. Each of the captured picture callbacks has
+six slices; the source helper validates their picture and parameter-set linkage.
+
+No captured bytes or private fixture paths are embedded in the source patch.
+The caller establishes archive authenticity; this script reports the supplied
+stream/records hashes and the current helper/header hashes. It proves host
+helper acceptance of those packet boundaries. It does not build the Android
+component, run a board workload, decode pixels, test Surface/MediaCodec/container
+integration, or measure encoder throughput.
