+# HEVC HDR parser and snapshot host tests
+
+From the source root, run:
+
+```sh
+sh tests/host/run_hevc_hdr.sh
+sh tests/host/run_hevc_hdr.sh --sanitize
+```
+
+The first command builds the C parser and C++17 metadata tracker with strict
+warnings. The second also enables AddressSanitizer and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer.
+`CC` and `CXX` select the host compilers. Temporary build files are removed on exit.
+If a restricted sandbox prevents LeakSanitizer from inspecting the process, use
+`--sanitize --no-lsan`; that switch disables leak checking for this host executable
+only, while address and undefined-behavior checks remain enabled.
+
+The test uses real encoded prefix SEI bytes with emulation prevention, plus hvcC
+and length-prefixed framing. It checks mastering metadata values, immutable
+snapshots for reordered frames, inherited stream metadata, malformed-input
+rollback, new-CSD and lifecycle resets, retained older snapshots, per-instance
+isolation, duplicate IDs, and the bounded 512-entry snapshot queue.
+
+These tests compile only the Android-independent parser/tracker. They do not
+compile the Codec2 interface, exercise the driver, verify framework reflection,
+or prove MediaCodec output-format behavior. Full matching Android compilation
+and device regression remain required. In particular, an HDR-to-SDR transition
+on the **same** codec instance must confirm that framework-cached
+`hdr-static-info` is cleared; tracker reset alone does not prove that transport
+behavior. Also test fresh SDR startup, reordered HDR output, flush/reset,
+new-CSD transitions, and output buffers held across codec destruction. The
+parser expects complete NAL/access-unit input; arbitrary NAL fragmentation is
+outside this source port's tested contract.
