+# HEVC level logic host checks
+
+Run from the Codec2 source root:
+
+```sh
+python3 tests/host/run_hevc_level_limits.py
+sh tests/host/run_color_conversion.sh
+```
+
+The level runner extracts the **current** Main-tier limit table,
+`fitsHEVCMainLevel`, maximum-framerate getter and level-IDC getter directly from
+`components/EncodeInterface.cpp`. It compiles those bodies using minimal
+symbolic C2 enum tags and class-field fixtures. The fixture enum numbers are
+not Android ABI values. This verifies the pure unit logic, not the complete
+`EncodeInterface` class, Android/C2 ABI, actual driver capabilities or hardware.
+
+Cases cover Main5 versus5.1 at4K30/40Mbps; normative64/65fps boundaries;
+per-axis and coding-block rounding; zero/extreme dimensions; NaN/infinite rates;
+bitrate boundaries; the explicit30fps/3840x2160 implementation policy; optional
+queried-rate reduction; invalid/missing state; and all13 `general_level_idc`
+mappings. These limits still must be intersected with driver-enumerated levels.
+
+The default build uses ASan and UBSan. LeakSanitizer is disabled because some
+sandboxes cannot enumerate proc task lists. `--no-sanitize` is available on
+hosts without sanitizer runtimes. `--cxx PATH` selects a compiler executable.
+The generated source and binary live in a scoped temporary directory that is
+removed after the run. The source SHA256 is printed so the result identifies
+the version of `EncodeInterface.cpp` that was tested.
